# Backend (Laravel)

## API-first

- Every public and admin action has a proper JSON API under `/api/v1/...`.
- Controllers return the standard envelope (`success`, `data`, `message`, `errors`). Do not invent ad-hoc shapes.
- New features: migrations + models + policies/middleware + routes + feature tests. No “controller-only” shortcuts.

## Auth & tenancy

- Sanctum/cookie auth for dashboard; public routes use `public.tenant` (Host-based tenant resolution).
- Never skip auth checks for convenience. Gate admin and setup flows consistently with middleware.
- Tenant-scoped queries only — never leak another tenant’s data.

## Modules

- Backend code for a product area lives under `backend/modules/{slug}/` (or the established module path for that slug).
- Third-party APIs (Zarinpal, Digipay, ERP sync, etc.) stay inside that module’s services — not in a global “helpers dump”.

## Documentation (mandatory)

- Every new or changed endpoint must be documented in Docusaurus:
  - English: `docs-site/docs/`
  - Persian: `docs-site/i18n/fa/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/`
- Document method, path, auth, request/response examples, and error codes.

```text
❌ BAD — merge API without docs
✅ GOOD — OpenAPI/docs page + FA translation for the same endpoint
```

## Docker

- Production PHP image: `docker/php/Dockerfile.platform`.
- Keep `.env` secrets out of images; compose mounts `backend/.env`.
